WEBVTT

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.860
I knew I was right.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.600
Where did you plant the bomb?

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.330
I don't know what
you're talking about.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.700
You are very brave to say that.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.360
Okay then, I'll try the hard way.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.100
I want to see you but I can't
see you because it hurts so much.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:58.200
I'm sure I must
be missing something...

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.500
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.600
(Yami, the Hat and the Book traveler)
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:12.530
I had always believed
that what I saw before me...

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:19.330
...was the only truth there was.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:27.160
But now I know
there isn't just one world.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:36.630
There are a thousand worlds called
"if" and I don't know which way to turn.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:42.530
I want to see you but
I can't see you; where are you now?

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:45.660
I'll find you no matter the cost.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:53.430
I've wandered into the
labyrinth of your eyes.

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:57.360
Even if the darkness bars my path...

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:03.430
...even if my weak heart
is led astray, I won't give up.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:08.400
I'll keep searching for you.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.960
Youko

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.960
If you don't cooperate,
your body will experience pain.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.030
Do you not care?

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:04.830
Why do we have to be
in such a cold place?

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.260
It's much nicer and
bigger than the other place...

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.330
...and we get a nice view, too.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:14.860
It's too dark to see anything.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:20.760
Watching the snow fall
like this... it's so much fun.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:30.900
No way. It's so cold and dark
here, how could you say it's fun?

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:36.460
It really is cold.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:41.160
Look, it's cold
enough to freeze sake!

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.630
What are you doing?

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:51.560
It's not funny, honey! You gotta
stop, please! Help my god, buddha!

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:57.630
Oh, Ken got frozen.

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.030
How about a drink, missy?

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:51.800
No thanks.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:02.000
Hey, what's going on?
You seem to be in a hurry.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:05.760
Nothing's wrong.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:10.860
Everybody's in a big hurry, huh!

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.630
Thank you!

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:31.100
What's that?

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:36.000
Will you buy something?
I am having a slow day.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:37.330
Nope.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:38.800
Stingy passenger.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:41.160
I didn't expect too much anyway.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:42.430
See ya!

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.930
Oh, do you know
Hatsumi by any chance?

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.830
Maybe... in here!

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:02.900
That's not funny.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.630
It's kind of true, isn't it?

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.100
Hey, what is this?

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:13.560
You're not so bad, I give up.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.360
Where did the captain go?

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.430
The guy who told us to check
must have something to do with it.

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:43.600
Let's find him.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:47.230
You want me to find a
guy at the dining car?

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:07.630
Excuse me, I am in the next room
and my partner is having stomach pain.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:12.430
So, I am asking around to see if
anybody can spare some medicine?

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.760
It must be serious.

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:18.600
Yes.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.730
This way.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:21.700
Nobody's here.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:24.330
It must be him.

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:26.230
We have to find him.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:31.630
This doesn't really seem to
be about your friend's sickness.

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:35.900
If you can't help, I'll excuse
myself. Thank you anyway.

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:39.930
If you go out now, you
will be in bigger trouble.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:42.900
...Miss.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:44.330
What?

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.200
Those breasts
are too big to hide.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.500
It's so obvious.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:08:00.600
I heard that there's a better way
for a woman to dress as a man.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:04.130
How dare you... who are you?

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:09.300
My god, it's my lucky day to meet
someone with the same background.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:28.260
There's someone
I want you to meet.

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:30.300
Care to come with me?

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:41.360
Someone for me to meet?

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:43.930
Okay then.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:48.400
Come in.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.500
I appreciate you letting
me borrow this dress.

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:03.130
No problem, it's
just a business sample.

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:06.800
And you look much
better in this outfit anyway.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.360
Tiger of Siberia, who is this?

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.830
Your kind of friend.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:16.800
Why did you make
direct contact with me?

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:18.400
I'm sorry.

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:21.500
I told her to do so.

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:24.860
I thought it would be best
under the given circumstances.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:29.500
It's better to know each other's
backgrounds to proceed wisely.

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:31.330
That's my feeling.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.160
But...

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:38.160
You cannot survive if you
only act by the book or by order.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:51.900
Hey, let's drink together!
Anybody in there?

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:57.100
Let's drink together,
I know someone's in there!

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:59.400
Sir, please stop that,
go back to your seat.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:03.060
Shut up! That's how you
treat a first class passenger?

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:06.560
You are causing a
lot of trouble, please!

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:12.530
Sorry, we are having a business
meeting, please don't disturb us.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.960
What did you just say?

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:18.500
Sir, please!

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:27.660
What kind of
business meeting is this?

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.260
Mister!

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:35.700
Give me the signal code book.

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:37.100
You!

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:40.760
Keep quiet, gentlemen.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:43.230
You, too!?

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:46.960
Just a conductor and a drunk.

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:53.600
It was good that I had a
back up plan as insurance.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:55.800
Back up?

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:58.530
I placed a time bomb on this train.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:02.760
If I don't re-set the time bomb,...

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:06.800
...the train will blow up
and the signal code will be lost.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:10.660
If I die, everything
will be gone, too.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:14.560
Shit, don't mess
with me, pretty boy!

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:17.000
Don't make a move!

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.800
This chick is next.

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:28.060
Are you okay with that?

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:47.030
Hey, get a hold of yourself!

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:52.460
Look after the signal code book...

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:56.830
Where is it? Hey!

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:30.100
It was when I thought of
creating the blue sky in Arcadia...

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:39.700
...I thought that there must be
a garden filled with sun flowers.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:49.530
And, also a church
amongst the sun flowers.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:51.860
Yes, indeed...

00:12:52.730 --> 00:13:00.830
That means... you all still
wish to build the city with me?

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:03.400
Of course.

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:06.830
Oh, that's odd.

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:13.300
You promised me that you
would absolutely bring Eve,...

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:19.600
...the essence of this land,
the next time you came.

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:27.630
No no, sir, I didn't mean
absolutely or by all means...

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:30.360
That hurts!

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:35.800
If we bring Eve here, this
land will grow so much better!

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:45.900
Then... why don't we have Eve?

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.760
I--I am sorry, sir...

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:50.830
Master Gargantua...

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:58.060
If you lose your temper,
it's not good for your skin.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:02.430
Seiren, sorry to make you worry.

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:06.160
So, I came up with the idea.

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:11.330
Seiren help us!

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:13.700
What's the matter?

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:16.000
Nothing.

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:23.730
As you all know,
Seiren is pure youma.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:28.660
She can help us find Eve!

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:35.060
Well, let's us return to the
story of night train, shall we?

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:40.330
What's going on in there?

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:47.330
Oh my, what happened?

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:57.400
Well well, those fools...

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:59.460
I-I thought you got shot?

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:01.760
How could you kill them
before getting the information?

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:05.600
Well, I get the idea anyway.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:06.760
What?

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:08.600
Don't you get it?

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:13.500
This soldier and
conductor are my men.

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:16.930
Aren't you the
"Tiger of Siberia"?

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:21.400
Yes, there was a
time I called myself that.

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:24.660
But, times have changed.

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:29.400
Even now a third-rate
person like him can be a spy.

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:42.800
I'll be your match.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:49.530
But miss, you really
look good in that dress.

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:04.660
The most required skill in this
business is not youth nor strength.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:07.130
It's... experience!

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:24.460
I know exactly
where the code book is.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:57.030
Hand over what that
young man gave you earlier.

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:08.530
Time is running out. If you
obey me, you won't get hurt.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:18.860
Where did you hide it?!

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:22.160
It must be...

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:28.460
Die already!

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:54.230
Payback time!

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:16.360
The time bomb!

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:20.030
A man gave you something, right?

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:29.960
That man who gave that to
you set a time bomb on this train.

00:18:30.930 --> 00:18:32.760
Do you remember
anything about him?

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:38.260
He... came out of the
restroom in the 1st class car.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:39.360
Let's go.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:50.760
It's not here.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.660
When he came out...

00:18:56.060 --> 00:18:57.530
...he was brushing
something off his shoulder.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:01.030
Snow?

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:25.860
Found it!

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:39.630
What's wrong? You found it.

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:42.060
It's empty.

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:43.030
Nothing's in it.

00:19:43.960 --> 00:19:45.960
Why, why is there nothing in it!?

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:48.930
I have no idea.

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:55.760
Oh, here you are...
where have you been?

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:57.500
That is...

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.200
Oh this?

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:02.000
Just before...

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:05.860
What's that?

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:17.630
Okay, it's opened.

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:21.330
Oh, I found a watch!

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:22.360
Lucky me!

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:24.430
The time bomb!?

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:48.430
Why did you help me?

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:50.830
To protect myself.

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:52.500
That's it.

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:54.100
That's it?

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:57.360
Because you're a good person.

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:02.560
A good person? That's not a
compliment to me, but thanks anyway.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:05.930
See you.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:17.060
Hazuki, come on!

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:19.160
We have no business
in this world any more.

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:22.860
How long can this search go on?

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:27.400
We must find Eve, or I won't last.

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:31.930
I ain't as young as
I look, you got that!?

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:53.360
I will offer up an eternal prayer.

00:21:53.630 --> 00:21:59.800
I will never give up on what matters.

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:07.260
I will go there, praying.

00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:14.100
No matter the distance
between us, I will catch you.

00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:21.930
That's a promise between you and I.

00:22:22.130 --> 00:22:29.260
Crying, cradling my memories,...

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.760
...won't help even one
of my feelings to reach you.

00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:44.800
I will offer up an eternal prayer.

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:51.430
I will never give up on what matters.

00:22:53.400 --> 00:23:00.330
I will find the dawn
between you and I,...

00:23:01.130 --> 00:23:08.760
...and meet the approaching daybreak.

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:14.000
I will go there, praying.

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:18.800
Big head girl wasn't
in the night train book.

00:23:19.430 --> 00:23:20.660
Oh my...

00:23:21.100 --> 00:23:23.030
Let's take a look
at the next book.

00:23:49.730 --> 00:23:53.200
Next Time: Jill
Yami the Hat and the Book Traveler

00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:56.260
We hope you
enjoy the next story.
